 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GMD</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the conversion of GDP-D-mannose to GDP-4-dehydro-6-deoxy-D-mannose.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=GDP-alpha-D-mannose = GDP-4-dehydro-alpha-D-rhamnose +H2O; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:23820, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:57527,ChEBI:CHEBI:57964; EC=4.2.1.47;COFACTOR:Name=NADP(+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:58349;Evidence={ECO:0000269|Ref.9};PATHWAY: Nucleotide-sugar biosynthesis; GDP-L-fucose biosynthesisvia de novo pathway; GDP-L-fucose from GDP-alpha-D-mannose: step1/2.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=O60547-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=O60547-2; Sequence=VSP_047324;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;SIMILARITY: Belongs to the NAD(P)-dependent epimerase/dehydratasefamily. GDP-mannose 4,6-dehydratase subfamily. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=AAC24501.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Note=Translation N-terminally extended.; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
